or both generation and browser rendering.\",\n    \"code_snippet\": \"(string-append\\n  result\\n  \\\"  <text x=\\\\\\\"\\\" (number->string (* x char-width)) \\\"\\\\\\\"\\\"\\n  \\\" y=\\\\\\\"\\\" (number->string (* (+ y 1) char-height)) \\\"\\\\\\\"\\\"\\n  ... \\\">\\\" (char->svg-safe ch) \\\"</text>\\\\n\\\")\",\n    \"suggested_fix\": \"Group characters into a single <text> element using <tspan> with relative offsets, or use a single <text> element with preserved whitespace if using a monospace font.\",\n    \"confidence\": 0.8,\n    \"category\": \"performance\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"shell/fuel/adaptive-allocator.ss\",\n    \"severity\": \"low\",\n    \"line\": 80,\n    \"description\": \"'allocator-push-observation' uses 'take' which is O(N) where N is 'max-history'. This is called on every observation update, resulting in O(HistorySize) overhead per observation.\",\n    \"code_snippet\": \"[new-history (if (>= len max-h)\\n                 (cons obs (take history (- max-h 1)))\\n                 (cons obs history))]\",\n    \"suggested_fix\": \"Use a ring buffer (vector with a pointer) to store observations in O(1) time.\",\n    \"confidence\": 0.75,\n    \"category\": \"performance\"\n  }\n]\n```",
